                                                              "summary":  "Brown\u0027s thesis is that AI infrastructure demand is being systematically underestimated because observers benchmark it against today\u0027s familiar use casesÃƒÂ¢Ã¢â€šÂ¬Ã¢â‚¬Âchatbots and searchÃƒÂ¢Ã¢â€šÂ¬Ã¢â‚¬Ârather than the autonomous agent world coming next. He argues that a billion people each with a personal AI agent, plus autonomous vehicles, robots, and continuous machine-to-machine computation, will require orders of magnitude more compute than exists today. Tech leaders are not worried about overbuilding data centers; they are worried about not building fast enough.",
