                                                              "date":  "2026-09-15",
                                                              "imageUrl":  null,
                                                              "summary":  "Santoli argues that AI has exited its euphoric early phase, when nearly every bet on the theme produced winners. The narrative has shifted toward riskÃƒÂ¢Ã¢â€šÂ¬Ã¢â‚¬Âpublic skepticism about the technology has grown, and visibility into order backlogs and capex returns beyond a few quarters is now seriously questioned. However, mega-cap tech platforms like Microsoft, Alphabet, and Meta have room to pace their capital deployment more sustainably. He frames this maturation not as a collapse but as a necessary transition to a more selective, risk-aware phase of the AI trade.",
                                                              "take":  "Santoli is correctly marking the end of a trade, not the end of a trend. The first phase of AI investing was easy: buy anything with AI exposure and win. That is over. The second phase rewards companies that can demonstrate actual revenue conversion and defensible margins from their AI investmentsÃƒÂ¢Ã¢â€šÂ¬Ã¢â‚¬Âand punishes those that cannot. For investors, this means the AI basket trade is dead and stock selection within AI is now the game. Companies that have absorbed massive capex and can show it in earnings will re-rate higher; those that cannot will face a prolonged de-rating.",
