                                                                                "summary":  "Santoli examines the post-summer state of the bull market, noting the S\u0026P 500 has done just enough to preserve its upward path after a brief late-summer pullback that approached but never breached its May-July trading range. Professional investor positioning data from Goldman Sachs, State Street, NAAIM, and Bank of America all show allocators are stocked up for the fall, with equity exposures and risk appetites near full. The XLK technology ETF emerges as the key indicator: its ability to break to new highs or stall in its recent range will likely determine whether the broader bull market has enough technical momentum to extend into year-end. The article notes that while seasonal patterns in September are historically weak, strong prior-year returns have historically moderated that effect.",
